VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to take you through it though, and I\'m I appreciate you going through it with me because I\'m really proud of this. &gt;&gt; [screaming] &gt;&gt; So, we\'re going to go through it. I\'m going to assume that you can go to the GitHub and see the installation instructions. I\'m not going to take you'

[00:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'through those, but I\'m going [music] to take you through the website, my thinking, my workflow, and how it works out. So, to start, my goal of writing this was because nothing else worked for what I wanted. I'

[01:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have Prusa printers, but Prusa Connect does not work well for what I need. Bamboo has a farm software as well. I think Grant at 3D Musketeers talked about a while'

[01:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ago. I I didn\'t get a chance to watch that video. My goal though was to be printer agnostic in a way and to just maximize throughput and be as efficient as possible. With the goal being that'

[01:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'our run of XRP kits for SparkFun, we could then use this tool that I\'ve created to be better about running it. The computer can keep track of counts,'

[01:49] [scene:talk]
