[14:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'little bit different. The idea is each class of machine has its own connector as a as a go-between. So, Print Farm functionality knows how to do this stuff. Connector knows how to talk to'

[14:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the 3D printer. They talk to each other. Below that is dispatch settings, and I have that set to five. And I did this because the networking on the Prusa machines can be flaky. And so, I found that if I do five at a time, I\'m not'

[15:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'overwhelming the network. I\'m not overwhelming 3D printers. I\'m not overwhelming the computer. What it will do is send jobs to the first five printers that it has available. And once those are printing, it\'ll then send it'

[15:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to the other five. And then the other five. And then another five, eventually filling up the farm. That\'s what the dispatch setting is. You can also back up your farm. It stores locally, again, locally on a machine, but it wouldn\'t'

